          "text": [
            "\n",
            "--- Summary of Model Performance (Test Set) ---\n",
            "Random Forest - RMSE: 0.6108, R²: 0.9120\n",
            "XGBoost       - RMSE: 0.6500, R²: 0.9003\n",
            "LSTM          - RMSE: 0.6321, R²: 0.9058\n",
            "\n",
            "--- Notes ---\n",
            "1. This notebook uses synthetic data. Real-world applications require actual GRACE data and relevant daily predictors (precipitation, temperature, etc.).\n",
            "2. Feature engineering is crucial. The current features are time-based. External physical drivers would significantly improve model performance.\n",
            "3. Chronological splitting for train/test is vital for time series to avoid data leakage.\n",
            "4. Hyperparameter tuning (e.g., GridSearchCV, KerasTuner) can optimize each model further.\n",
            "5. LSTM requires careful data preparation (scaling, sequencing). The test set for LSTM might be slightly smaller than for RF/XGBoost due to sequence creation if not handled carefully for alignment.\n",
            "6. Increased `end_year` for more data, especially beneficial for the LSTM model and robust train/test splits.\n"
